course: dictionary
lesson: 2919
title: Pipes that carry rain
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A drainpipe is a pipe on the outside of a building. It carries rainwater from the roof down to the ground or into a drain. «The rain ran off the roof and down the drainpipe.» Drain means to let water flow away, and a pipe is a tube, so a drainpipe is a tube that carries water away.
explain: Context gives you clues. «The blocked drainpipe overflowed onto the path.» Blocked means stopped up, so the water could not get through and spilled out. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Something that carries water away. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: The same word can have a different meaning. «Her drainpipe trousers were so narrow she could hardly bend.» These trousers are not pipes at all. They are very narrow trousers. The words around the word show you which meaning is right.
explain: In stories, characters sometimes climb down a drainpipe to escape. In real life this is very dangerous, so never try it. When you read a story, remember that the author may be making things up.
fact: A drainpipe is a pipe on the outside of a building that carries rainwater down.
fact: Drainpipe is a noun, and its plural is drainpipes.
fact: «Drainpipe trousers» means very narrow trousers, not a pipe.
fact: In 2016 an octopus called Inky was reported to have escaped from a New Zealand aquarium down a drainpipe into the sea.
fact: Climbing down a drainpipe is dangerous in real life, so do not copy stories like that.
exercise: «The rain ran down the drainpipe into the drain.» What is a drainpipe? | A small bird that lives near water | A metal ladder for climbing up walls | *A pipe on the outside of a building that carries rainwater down
exercise: «Her drainpipe trousers were so narrow she could hardly bend.» What does drainpipe mean here? | Very wide trousers with big pockets | Trousers with a hole in the knee | Trousers made of plastic pipe | *Very narrow trousers
exercise: «The blocked drainpipe overflowed onto the path.» Why would a blocked drainpipe be a problem? | It would make the rain taste sweet | *Rainwater could not get away and would spill over | It would make the birds sing louder | It would make the building taller
test: What does a drainpipe carry? | Air for the children to breathe | *Rainwater from the roof | Hot food to the kitchen | Sand from the beach
test: «Climbing down a drainpipe is dangerous, so never try it.» Why does the sentence say never try it? | Because drainpipes are too small to see | Because drainpipes are made of gold | *Because it is very dangerous in real life | Because drainpipes are too sticky to touch
exam: «A blocked drainpipe caused the flood, so the council sent workers to clear it.» What does blocked mean? | Very long and thin | *Stopped up, so water cannot get through | Painted bright red | Filled with sweets
